00:49:04.242 --> 00:49:05.963
install cordo as well.

00:49:05.963 --> 00:49:08.803
So we got that as well before that.

00:49:08.803 --> 00:49:09.722
But once you have those things,

00:49:09.722 --> 00:49:11.283
it should do what it says on the screen,

00:49:11.283 --> 00:49:13.323
basically show you stuff in the terminal,

00:49:13.323 --> 00:49:14.522
which is all positive.

00:49:14.522 --> 00:49:18.203
It's creating that great docs.yaml file.

00:49:18.203 --> 00:49:20.323
And it should be pretty minimal what's in there.

00:49:20.323 --> 00:49:22.602
It should actually also be a little bit dynamic.

00:49:22.602 --> 00:49:23.522
Based on your project,

00:49:23.522 --> 00:49:28.522
it'll craft like the correct great docs.yaml file

00:49:28.522 --> 00:49:30.083
or the config file.

00:49:30.083 --> 00:49:31.722
And then you could go ahead and customize,

00:49:31.722 --> 00:49:34.602
but you might just jump to building your documentation

00:49:34.602 --> 00:49:36.122
because that's the next easiest thing.

00:49:36.122 --> 00:49:38.522
It's just another command, great docs build.

00:49:39.362 --> 00:49:44.362
And what you get is a great hyphen docs directory

00:49:45.283 --> 00:49:46.882
in your working directory.

00:49:46.882 --> 00:49:49.122
And that contains like the site folder,

00:49:49.122 --> 00:49:50.443
but you don't really have to worry about that

00:49:50.443 --> 00:49:53.242
because you have another command called great docs preview,

00:49:53.242 --> 00:49:57.283
which will basically launch like a web server

00:49:57.283 --> 00:50:01.083
and then put the site in your default browser,

00:50:01.362 --> 00:50:04.522
basically just like let you see the site locally.

00:50:04.522 --> 00:50:05.923
And then because I'm a big fan

00:50:05.923 --> 00:50:07.163
of letting people know what's going on.

00:50:07.163 --> 00:50:08.642
So it should be totally a black box.

00:50:08.642 --> 00:50:11.122
I give on this page, like a structure,

00:50:11.122 --> 00:50:13.722
the basic structure of how it should look

00:50:13.722 --> 00:50:15.443
on your working directory.

00:50:16.563 --> 00:50:17.403
But that's kind of it.

00:50:17.403 --> 00:50:19.163
And I believe the next step for most people

00:50:19.163 --> 00:50:21.362
will just be getting this on CI if they're satisfied

00:50:21.362 --> 00:50:22.803
and then just working from there,

00:50:22.803 --> 00:50:25.203
like modifying their initialization,

00:50:25.203 --> 00:50:28.642
not initialization, their config file

00:50:28.642 --> 00:50:31.362
to give the site more customization personality

00:50:31.362 --> 00:50:35.083
and there'll be authoring guides and things like that.

00:50:35.083 --> 00:50:35.923
Very cool.

00:50:35.923 --> 00:50:39.362
So you've got the really nice watch feature.

00:50:39.362 --> 00:50:41.642
So great docs build dash dash watch.

00:50:41.642 --> 00:50:42.482
Yes.

